    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_d7d132af",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Propaganda; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a revolver placed on what appears to be the U.S. Constitution, with an American flag in the background. The text overlays claim that 'terrorist attacks innocent people with guns' and that 'leaders want innocent people to give up their guns and become even more defenseless.' This juxtaposition of imagery and text is designed to frame gun control as a threat to personal safety and national security, implicitly blaming government leaders for encouraging vulnerability. The overall intent is propagandistic: to sway public opinion by associating gun control with increased danger and to promote the idea that gun ownership is essential for self-defense against terrorism. The visual elements (gun, Constitution, flag) are used symbolically to evoke patriotism and the notion of individual rights, while the text attempts to create fear and justify resistance to gun regulation. This meme does not contain explicit hate or abuse toward specific protected groups, but it promotes a divisive political narrative that can be harmful by polarizing public discourse and potentially inciting violence or fear against those advocating for gun control.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_02c5702f"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
