      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "second_amendment",
      "label": "Second Amendment to the U.S. Constitution",
      "description": "The Second Amendment to the United States Constitution, ratified in 1791, protects the right of the people to keep and bear arms. It is often cited in arguments for gun ownership and resistance to gun control legislation. The image uses the Constitution as a symbolic backdrop to invoke this amendment.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
